# Frontend local-dev environment. Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) to override.
# These only affect `bun run dev` / Vite — production is served by the Go binary.

# ── Recommended: develop against your local Go server ────────────────────────
#
# 1. Follow CONTRIBUTING.md's "Dev setup" section to get `go run ./cmd/graph
#    serve` running on :8080 (docker compose up -d, migrate, create a user).
# 2. Run `bun run dev` — Vite proxies /api to that local server by default, no
#    .env.local needed for this path.

# ── API proxy target ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to the local Go server above.
# GRAPH_API_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# ── Alternative: target a real deployed instance directly ───────────────────
# Requires a valid session cookie (copy from DevTools → Application → Cookies
# on your instance's host) or, if it's behind an auth proxy that sets
# X-Auth-Request-Email (see deploy/README.md), a kubectl port-forward instead:
#
#      kubectl -n <namespace> port-forward deploy/graph-serve 8080:8080
#      GRAPH_DEV_EMAIL=you@example.com bun run dev
#
# GRAPH_API_TARGET=https://graph.example.com
# GRAPH_SESSION_COOKIE=
# GRAPH_DEV_EMAIL=
